{"type": "root", "attrs": {"type": "node", "context": "cop", "internal": "camerafrompoints", "since": "22.0", "version": null, "namespace": null}, "body": [{"level": 0, "type": "title", "indent": 0, "text": ["Camera From Points"], "extent": [76, 99]}, {"type": "summary", "indent": 0, "text": ["Solves for intrinsic and extrinsic camera properties given a \nset of image-world correspondences."], "extent": [99, 205]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 0, "text": ["This node solves for the aspect ratio, focal length, rotation, and absolute\nposition of a camera given a set of known 3D positions in world space and \ntheir corresponding 2D projections in image space. This is done using a\n", {"scheme": "Wp", "value": "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Perspective-n-Point", "type": "link", "text": ["Perspective-n-Point (PnP) algorithm"], "exists": true}, " in \nconjunction with ", {"scheme": "Wp", "value": "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Random_sample_consensus", "type": "link", "text": ["RANSAC"], "exists": true}, "\nfor filtering outliers."], "extent": [205, 631]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 0, "text": ["Use this node to recover a camera required to composite 3D elements into an\nimage, where details about the camera used to capture the image are incomplete\nor unknown."], "extent": [631, 799]}, {"level": 1, "id": "parameters", "container": true, "type": "parameters_section", "indent": 0, "role": "section", "extent": [799, 811], "body": [{"type": "parameters_item_group", "body": [{"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 0, "text": ["Signature"], "extent": [811, 823], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["The layer type that the source accepts."], "extent": [847, 892]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["See ", {"scheme": null, "value": "/copernicus/glossary#signatures", "type": "link", "text": ["Signatures"], "fullpath": "/copernicus/glossary.html#signatures", "fragment": "#signatures"}, " for more information."], "extent": [892, 968]}], "container": true, "attrs": {"id": "signature"}, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 0, "text": ["World Point Attribute"], "extent": [968, 991], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["The point attribute on ", {"type": "code", "text": ["matches"]}, " containing the world space coordinate\n    of a point."], "extent": [1017, 1109]}], "container": true, "attrs": {"id": "worldattrib"}, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 0, "text": ["Image Point Attribute"], "extent": [1109, 1132], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["The point attribute on ", {"type": "code", "text": ["matches"]}, " containing the image space coordinate\n    of a point."], "extent": [1158, 1250]}], "container": true, "attrs": {"id": "worldattrib"}, "role": "item"}], "container": true, "role": "item_group"}, {"level": 2, "id": null, "container": true, "type": "h", "indent": 0, "text": ["Camera Intrinsics"], "extent": [1250, 1274], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 0, "text": ["If the camera intrinsic parameters are known, they can be set manually \nso that they do not need to be estimated by the solver. "], "extent": [1274, 1405]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 0, "text": ["By default, the projective center of the image is assumed to be at the \nnumerical center of the image. For cropped images, this assumption can\nbe incorrect and give unreliable solutions. In this case, it is worthwhile\nto calibrate the projective center accurately.  "], "extent": [1405, 1673]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 0, "text": ["The center can be estimated using the orthocenter theorem. This requires\ntwo lines to define an axis vanishing point. Exactly three mutually orthogonal \naxes must be defined explicitly to recover the projective center."], "extent": [1673, 1893]}, {"type": "parameters_item_group", "body": [{"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 0, "text": ["Edit Intrinsics"], "extent": [1893, 1910], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Enable the use of known camera intrinsics."], "extent": [1942, 1990]}], "container": true, "attrs": {"id": "enableknownintrinsics"}, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 0, "text": ["Focal Length"], "extent": [1990, 2004], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["The camera focal length to use if this parameter is enabled. When disabled, \n    the PnP solver will estimate this parameter with the assumption that the \n    aperture is ", {"type": "code", "text": ["2"]}, "."], "extent": [2020, 2201]}], "container": true, "attrs": {"id": "focal"}, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 0, "text": ["Camera Center"], "extent": [2201, 2216], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["The method used to set the projective center if this parameter is enabled.\n    When disabled, the center is assumed to be at the image origin."], "extent": [2239, 2387]}, {"type": "dt_group", "body": [{"type": "dt", "indent": 4, "text": ["Image Center"], "extent": [2387, 2405], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 8, "text": ["Manually set the image space coordinate of the\n        projective center."], "extent": [2405, 2488]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 4, "text": ["Use Estimator"], "extent": [2488, 2507], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 8, "text": ["Use an orthocenter image estimator to recover the projective\n        center of the image if it is unknown."], "extent": [2507, 2623]}], "container": true}], "container": true}], "container": true, "attrs": {"id": "cameracenter"}, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 0, "text": ["Image Center"], "extent": [2623, 2637], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["A vector specifying the image space coordinate of the \n    projective center."], "extent": [2659, 2742]}], "container": true, "attrs": {"id": "imagecenter"}, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 0, "text": ["Parallel Lines"], "extent": [2742, 2758], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Number of axis definitions."], "extent": [2782, 2815]}], "container": true, "attrs": {"id": "parallellines"}, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 0, "text": ["Line A#"], "extent": [2815, 2824], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["The first line used to define an axis, defined by a start and end \n    point in image coordinates."], "extent": [2841, 2945]}], "container": true, "attrs": {"id": "linea#"}, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 0, "text": ["Line B#"], "extent": [2945, 2954], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["The second line used to define an axis, defined by a start and end \n    point in image coordinates."], "extent": [2971, 3076]}], "container": true, "attrs": {"id": "lineb#"}, "role": "item"}], "container": true, "role": "item_group"}]}, {"level": 2, "id": null, "container": true, "type": "h", "indent": 0, "text": ["Advanced Settings"], "extent": [3076, 3100], "body": [{"type": "parameters_item_group", "body": [{"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 0, "text": ["RANSAC Seed"], "extent": [3100, 3114], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["The seed used to randomly select candidate point correspondences used\n    to solve for a camera."], "extent": [3135, 3237]}], "container": true, "attrs": {"id": "ransacseed"}, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 0, "text": ["RANSAC Iterations"], "extent": [3237, 3256], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["The number of RANSAC loop iterations executed to solve for a camera. \n    Increasing this can improve the accuracy of the solution."], "extent": [3282, 3419]}], "container": true, "attrs": {"id": "ransaciterations"}, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 0, "text": ["RANSAC Tolerance"], "extent": [3419, 3437], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["The reprojection error tolerance used to determine if a camera solution \n    is acceptable."], "extent": [3463, 3560]}], "container": true, "attrs": {"id": "ransactolerance"}, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 0, "text": ["Subset Mode"], "extent": [3560, 3573], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["The method used to select the size of the subset of points which \n    RANSAC should use to generate a candidate solution for the camera. By \n    default, this node uses a fixed count of 7 point correspondences."], "extent": [3593, 3809]}, {"type": "dt_group", "body": [{"type": "dt", "indent": 4, "text": ["Percentage of Input Points"], "extent": [3809, 3841], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 8, "text": ["Set the solver to use a percentage of the total point correspondences \n        in ", {"type": "code", "text": ["matches"]}, ". This is set in ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Percentage"]}, "."], "extent": [3841, 3974]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 4, "text": ["Count"], "extent": [3974, 3985], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 8, "text": ["Set the solver to use as an absolute number of point \n        correspondences. This is set in ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Count"]}, "."], "extent": [3985, 4099]}], "container": true}], "container": true}], "container": true, "attrs": {"id": "subsetmode"}, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 0, "text": ["Percentage"], "extent": [4099, 4111], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["If enabled, this is the percentage of point correspondences used in the\n    RANSAC solver. The percentage of selected points must evaluate to at least 7."], "extent": [4135, 4294]}], "container": true, "attrs": {"id": "subsetpercent"}, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 0, "text": ["Count"], "extent": [4294, 4301], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["If enabled, this is the number of point correspondences used in the \n    RANSAC solver. This number must be at least 7."], "extent": [4323, 4448]}], "container": true, "attrs": {"id": "subsetcount"}, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 0, "text": ["PnP Reprojection Error"], "extent": [4448, 4472], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["The reprojection error tolerance used to determine if a camera solution \n    is acceptable when assuming camera intrinsics, which is required if \n    the number of point correspondences is less than 7 but at least 3."], "extent": [4500, 4722]}], "container": true, "attrs": {"id": "reprojectionerror"}, "role": "item"}, {"type": "parameters_item", "indent": 0, "text": ["Apply Estimated Intrinsics"], "extent": [4722, 4750], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Set the solved aspect ratio, aperture, and focal length on ", {"type": "code", "text": ["camera"]}, "."], "extent": [4780, 4854]}], "container": true, "attrs": {"id": "applyintrinsics"}, "role": "item"}], "container": true, "role": "item_group"}]}], "text": "Parameters"}, {"level": 1, "id": "inputs", "container": true, "type": "inputs_section", "indent": 0, "role": "section", "extent": [4854, 4862], "body": [{"type": "dt_group", "body": [{"type": "dt", "indent": 4, "text": ["matches"], "extent": [4862, 4875], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 8, "text": ["Image-world point correspondences identified by attribute names \n        specified in ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["World Point Attribute"]}, " and ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Image Point \n        Attribute"]}, "."], "extent": [4875, 5036]}], "container": true}, {"type": "dt", "indent": 4, "text": ["layer"], "extent": [5036, 5047], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 8, "text": ["Layer onto which solved camera parameters are applied."], "extent": [5047, 5111]}], "container": true}], "container": true}], "text": "Inputs"}, {"level": 1, "id": "outputs", "container": true, "type": "outputs_section", "indent": 0, "role": "section", "extent": [5111, 5120], "body": [{"type": "dt_group", "body": [{"type": "dt", "indent": 4, "text": ["camera"], "extent": [5120, 5132], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 8, "text": ["The solved camera."], "extent": [5132, 5160]}], "container": true}], "container": true}], "text": "Outputs"}, {"level": 1, "id": "related", "container": true, "type": "related_section", "indent": 0, "role": "section", "extent": [5160, 5169], "body": [{"type": "bullet_group", "body": [{"blevel": 2, "type": "bullet", "indent": 0, "text": [{"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop/neural_layertodepth_moge2", "type": "link", "text": "", "fullpath": "/nodes/cop/neural_layertodepth_moge2.html"}], "extent": [5169, 5209]}], "container": true}], "text": "Related"}], "title": ["Camera From Points"], "summary": ["Solves for intrinsic and extrinsic camera properties given a \nset of image-world correspondences."]}